---
type: readme
title: ChromeOS Display Resolution Checker README
summary: Explains that the tool checks whether a new display panel satisfies the ChromeOS PPI requirement and that its conditions must stay in sync with the spec in ui/display/manager, including exceptions like Nocturne's 2.25x scale factor.
---

This page is used to check if a new panel satisfies the ChromeOS PPI(PixelPerInch)
equirement. The condition must be in sync with the spec implemented in
i/display/manager as there are several exceptions (such as we use 2.25x only for
Nocturne's 3000x2000 panel).


